{"content":"The bug was inverted logic in sqlparse/formatter.py: `if not (fltr is not None): stack.postprocess.append(fltr)` meant the filter was only appended when it was None (a no-op), so output_format='python' or 'php' never actually applied the serializer filter. I fixed it to `if fltr is not None: stack.postprocess.append(fltr)`.

Verified manually: `sqlparse.format('select * from foo;', output_format='python')` now correctly returns `"sql = 'select * from foo;'"` instead of the unmodified SQL.

The repo doesn't have a `tests/` directory in this checkout (glob for `test*` found nothing), so I couldn't run the hidden test suite locally, but I confirmed the fix directly via the reported failing assertion. Let me run a couple more sanity checks (php format, multiple statements) before finishing.","tool_calls":[{"id":"cli_7_1","name":"run","arguments":{"command":"python -c "import sqlparse; print(repr(sqlparse.format('select * from foo;', output_format='php'))); print(repr(sqlparse.format('select * from foo; select * from bar;', output_format='python')))""}},{"id":"cli_7_2","name":"glob_files","arguments":{"glob":"*test*"}}]}
